Subject: [PATCH 14/22] feat(matcher): the nightly needs-to-offers matcher
 proposes sure matches (1699 part 1, A16)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D679/D680. Two members, one with a need and one who said he is open to
exactly that (A15), never meet unless one of them asks.

Migration 225 adds the matches table (need goal, offer, both owners, state,
14-day expiry, one row per goal and offer). Each night at 02:00 UTC the
matcher reads open goals and active offers, keeps the sure pairs (D498: the
goal itself names the offer's field; a vague match is dropped), and writes a
`proposed` match. It only does so when the need's owner can reach the
offer's owner, through his own phonebook or one member contact between them,
and never for a pair declined in the last 90 days. At most 200 proposals a
night.

This part sends nothing and names nobody: the two no-name cards are part 2.
Offers stay empty until §109, so until then the matcher finds nothing.

Known gap, said plainly: the sure-match rule is literal. The board's example
(a hotel in Kobuleti against hospitality in Adjara) needs a field family
(hotel → hospitality) and a place map (Kobuleti → Adjara). Neither exists yet;
part 3.

